      "id": 1,
      "text": "Fredericksburg was founded on May 8, 1846 by German immigrants under the Society for the Protection of German Immigrants in Texas.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.fbgtx.org/208/History",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was named after Prince Frederick of Prussia, with the original spelling Friedrichsburg before changing to Fredericksburg.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fredericksburg%2C_Texas",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The first electric‑light company appeared in 1896 and the first ice factory opened in 1907, marking early industrial progress.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.fbgtx.org/208/History",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Enchanted Rock, a 27‑mile‑north granite monolith, sits just outside Fredericksburg and was declared a National Natural Landmark in 1970.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fredericksburg%2C_Texas",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Gillespie County Historical Society preserves the town’s heritage through its museum and community events.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
